{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "Sometimes you need to tag your models with tokens, think tagging images with keywords or including hashtags in a twitter post.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1d9d838f477e6e208c300459031e5b7df31c2a04bdce6703827fddca93e3667f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.5], [1, 0.5, 0.72], [2, 0.72, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.36], [6, 1.36, 1.64], [7, 1.64, 1.88], [8, 1.88, 2.2], [9, 2.56, 2.98], [10, 2.98, 3.44], [11, 3.44, 3.68], [12, 3.68, 3.98], [13, 3.98, 4.36], [14, 4.36, 4.68], [15, 4.68, 5.06], [16, 5.06, 5.56], [17, 5.56, 5.86], [18, 5.86, 5.94], [19, 5.94, 6.14], [20, 6.14, 6.52]]}, {"text": "And in a slightly more rare situation, you sometimes may want to have multiple types of tags for your products.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/05fbbafe24fb9e2464b488c4502bedd6bfe01e0ec18bc9faac1285edd381d705.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.0, 0.2], [2, 0.2, 0.3], [3, 0.3, 0.58], [4, 0.58, 0.86], [5, 0.86, 1.06], [6, 1.06, 1.76], [7, 2.04, 2.08], [8, 2.08, 2.44], [9, 2.44, 2.84], [10, 2.84, 3.08], [11, 3.08, 3.24], [12, 3.24, 3.44], [13, 3.44, 3.86], [14, 3.86, 4.3], [15, 4.3, 4.46], [16, 4.46, 4.72], [17, 4.72, 4.96], [18, 4.96, 5.06], [19, 5.06, 5.4]]}, {"text": "Like in an ecommerce store, you may want to have a style, color, type, or generic tags attached to your product model.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5feeacb0ab977af811cdd3ac1e558b0ac805d8439a76d0cd5509d83e90ffe333.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.56], [4, 0.98, 1.36], [5, 1.76, 1.88], [6, 1.88, 2.02], [7, 2.02, 2.24], [8, 2.24, 2.28], [9, 2.28, 2.42], [10, 2.42, 2.52], [11, 2.52, 2.88], [12, 3.24, 3.5], [13, 3.88, 4.08], [14, 4.46, 4.56], [15, 4.56, 4.88], [16, 4.88, 5.22], [17, 5.22, 5.7], [18, 5.7, 6.0], [19, 6.0, 6.04], [20, 6.04, 6.32], [21, 6.32, 6.72]]}, {"text": "These tags could be used in an recommendation engine to help determine what products are similar to other products.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f2186446666d23e7f23a43dcbab409462cf22897a34b2f9a71062808922b11b1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.12], [5, 1.12, 1.3], [7, 1.4, 1.84], [8, 1.84, 2.38], [9, 2.38, 2.66], [10, 2.66, 2.76], [11, 2.76, 3.12], [12, 3.12, 3.44], [13, 3.44, 3.8], [14, 3.8, 4.04], [15, 4.04, 4.36], [16, 4.36, 4.58], [17, 4.58, 4.76], [18, 4.76, 5.16]]}, {"text": "Create the Style Model", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3695add9dfec3b51c26c9b672946cf192c2b4a1f015eb176cfdea51d1c3bac52.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.34], [1, 0.34, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.84], [3, 0.84, 1.16]]}, {"text": "This is your basic many to many relationship between your style model and your products model.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/316fa828bce1694198381bc5139c5c5629e1396e3553c7302128b35107966412.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.46], [3, 0.46, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 1.12], [5, 1.12, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.5], [7, 1.5, 2.04], [8, 2.04, 2.4], [9, 2.4, 2.56], [10, 2.56, 2.88], [11, 2.88, 3.2], [12, 3.2, 3.68], [13, 3.68, 3.8], [14, 3.8, 4.12], [15, 4.12, 4.5]]}, {"text": "```ruby db/migrations/create_styles_table.rb", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d5f7d9bebc30ed26162ff8f2bcded5c1b8ce2a63336c09eeb5cf5eb7794e75fa.mp3"}, {"text": "Creating the tags concern", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6b9a8d7cc5d5859c382b47c2c4cd42fc18e655f2d4895405f187c657093a019a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.56], [2, 0.56, 0.84], [3, 0.84, 1.22]]}, {"text": "Because effectively all of the tags are going to have the same attributes (namely :name), I want to have all of that common code in a Concern that will be included in all of the different types of tags", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/566b51337f9677aa2ed18dbd3d1cd7586a7361a2a9fea82973304646b5a2db69.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.84], [2, 0.84, 1.18], [3, 1.18, 1.32], [4, 1.32, 1.48], [5, 1.48, 1.72], [6, 1.72, 2.04], [7, 2.04, 2.28], [8, 2.28, 2.46], [9, 2.46, 2.58], [10, 2.58, 2.74], [11, 2.74, 3.0], [12, 3.0, 3.52], [13, 3.94, 4.2], [15, 5.18, 5.38], [16, 5.38, 5.54], [17, 5.54, 5.68], [18, 5.68, 5.8], [19, 5.8, 6.04], [20, 6.04, 6.2], [21, 6.2, 6.3], [22, 6.3, 6.66], [23, 6.66, 7.0], [25, 7.26, 7.34], [26, 7.34, 7.7], [27, 7.7, 7.96], [28, 7.96, 8.08], [29, 8.08, 8.2], [30, 8.2, 8.58], [31, 8.58, 8.78], [32, 8.78, 9.0], [33, 9.0, 9.14], [34, 9.14, 9.2], [35, 9.2, 9.44], [36, 9.44, 9.74], [37, 9.74, 10.0], [38, 10.0, 10.42]]}, {"text": "My concern looks like this", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f9252adc12b9d83f9575b07ad60a7d76b00ee9dfa3f31c2cc47e067467fae9b9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.24]]}, {"text": "```ruby app/models/concerns/taggable.rb module Taggable extend ActiveSupport::Concern", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/475dc8fa348cc7327b4c2ff7ad9c924de5582cf7c23c4f855e3c24efcd16c3b2.mp3"}, {"text": "included do validate :name, presence: true", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/62ae01600a720a2f3ff431a3dd933f7af2aee6cb7e81905586f47a3b8806394a.mp3"}, {"text": "def downcase_name name.downcase!", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/954b72048649efd6318d8a475ec04a44df00fae52d7d079d80a92a9df1c56502.mp3"}, {"text": "end end", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e27042fefc1049473c3ac252d514dd62ad43d92d41c1c37a147db3ee441787ba.mp3"}, {"text": "Adding and removing tags", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5f84e1f6693697d64941be394ada36a9b32c80b0f53ab4b0b07614c7de695674.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.64], [2, 0.64, 1.0], [3, 1.0, 1.4]]}, {"text": "Using the jQuery tokenizer extension, you can follow the guide at Rails casts to hook into your model.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2d994124e836954e783b6fcfcd355d5c361426ba4402d9ef2013ee6a7ed6a7ab.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.5], [3, 1.04, 1.56], [4, 1.56, 2.02], [5, 2.52, 2.6], [6, 2.6, 2.72], [7, 2.72, 3.02], [8, 3.02, 3.22], [10, 3.44, 3.58], [11, 3.58, 3.74], [12, 3.74, 4.16], [13, 4.16, 4.5], [14, 4.5, 4.7], [15, 4.7, 4.9], [16, 4.9, 5.06], [17, 5.06, 5.32]]}, {"text": "While his approach is dandy and all, we have multiple types of tags attached to our product and there is a faster way to manage the addition methods on our model.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/406a44638b6748e93a48f0287fbb8f81152b41589559a041fc71d0ae7c8a8ac7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.44], [5, 1.44, 1.6], [6, 1.6, 1.8], [7, 2.12, 2.2], [8, 2.2, 2.34], [9, 2.34, 2.64], [10, 2.64, 3.02], [11, 3.02, 3.28], [12, 3.28, 3.56], [13, 3.56, 3.96], [14, 3.96, 4.28], [15, 4.28, 4.4], [16, 4.4, 4.8], [17, 5.02, 5.1], [18, 5.1, 5.26], [19, 5.26, 5.48], [20, 5.48, 5.6], [21, 5.6, 5.98], [22, 5.98, 6.18], [23, 6.18, 6.34], [24, 6.34, 6.68], [25, 6.68, 6.98], [26, 6.98, 7.28], [27, 7.28, 7.62], [28, 7.62, 7.9], [29, 7.9, 8.04], [30, 8.04, 8.32]]}, {"text": "His method requires that you have a method like below for every one of your token attributes.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/44579104461f7ceff8b3cac77f1175a0917cc868c25401fe19c81cd351e357ea.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.24], [4, 1.24, 1.36], [5, 1.36, 1.48], [6, 1.48, 1.6], [7, 1.6, 1.84], [8, 1.84, 2.06], [9, 2.06, 2.4], [10, 2.4, 2.72], [11, 2.72, 2.98], [12, 2.98, 3.14], [13, 3.14, 3.22], [14, 3.22, 3.34], [15, 3.34, 3.6], [16, 3.6, 4.08]]}, {"text": "This is going to make your products model huge as you add more and more taggable attributes.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/cdf98588f37035313c3d4fcd35fd0fcf1927cc93d45d0ff881a09593c5c2add6.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.7], [4, 0.7, 0.82], [5, 0.82, 0.98], [6, 0.98, 1.26], [7, 1.26, 1.6], [8, 1.6, 2.06], [9, 2.06, 2.3], [10, 2.3, 2.4], [11, 2.4, 2.62], [12, 2.62, 2.86], [13, 2.86, 3.14], [14, 3.14, 3.4], [16, 3.9, 4.38]]}, {"text": "```ruby app/models/concerns/taggable.rb has_and_belongs_to_many :authors", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/47b67b972a426e449869844bdf4d26877ed52d92468bc3b0e8040004bcf9e61f.mp3"}, {"text": "def author_tokens=(ids) self.author_ids = ids.split(“,”) end", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2402434fa38c6319602138a1ed1d6c9a292067a043fbfdd0fceac665d4d39c04.mp3"}, {"text": "Now as add more and more taggable items to the product model, it will automatically create the [attribute_name]_ids methods that the jQuery needs to attach these tokens onto our model.", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5de21653820c7a3dc601d3db87ade45c4726dd98668e734b18c27a57d20704db.mp3"}, {"text": "The more taggable attributes I add, the more code I save.", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a68ad4594d83a35a61df65e003e339a5f72679d78a717c38390d13cad37cf3ad.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.12], [1, 0.12, 0.3], [3, 0.8, 1.26], [4, 1.26, 1.52], [5, 1.52, 1.9], [6, 2.2, 2.3], [7, 2.3, 2.48], [8, 2.48, 2.74], [9, 2.74, 2.88], [10, 2.88, 3.18]]}, {"text": "Alternative approach", "block": 17, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ecd032c62b160fb1a15fd3fda8f6e230baf84b9c461e1200dd14ada4c9ed3d14.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.58], [1, 0.58, 1.18]]}, {"text": "You could argue that I could of put all of the tags in one table and used STI to break each type into different models.", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d824cbafa5733dc4fd6d8d4206d05e8b4bd69ef35a00fc706016e80487ce5c62.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.02], [5, 1.02, 1.18], [7, 1.34, 1.48], [8, 1.48, 1.72], [9, 1.72, 1.88], [10, 1.88, 1.98], [11, 1.98, 2.24], [12, 2.24, 2.42], [13, 2.42, 2.58], [14, 2.58, 2.92], [15, 2.92, 3.16], [16, 3.16, 3.42], [17, 3.42, 4.0], [18, 4.0, 4.2], [19, 4.2, 4.4], [20, 4.4, 4.72], [21, 4.72, 4.94], [22, 4.94, 5.28], [23, 5.28, 5.56], [24, 5.56, 5.96]]}, {"text": "While this could work if all of the tags had the same name type of string, you may want your name attribute to be an integer.", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/67fa7b8861c97945e9bfec883db82671125c843a2e73bbe722328ceb2a29ba11.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.14], [1, 0.14, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.5], [3, 0.5, 0.74], [4, 0.94, 1.04], [5, 1.04, 1.22], [6, 1.22, 1.36], [7, 1.36, 1.48], [8, 1.48, 1.74], [10, 1.94, 2.1], [11, 2.1, 2.34], [12, 2.34, 2.56], [13, 2.56, 2.84], [14, 2.84, 3.02], [15, 3.02, 3.26], [16, 3.74, 3.86], [17, 3.86, 4.02], [18, 4.02, 4.26], [19, 4.26, 4.4], [20, 4.4, 4.58], [21, 4.58, 5.1], [22, 5.1, 5.36], [23, 5.36, 5.5], [24, 5.5, 5.64], [25, 5.64, 6.04]]}, {"text": "Having them in separate tables will also reduce the table size, thus making the results run a little bit quicker.", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2d3abfa7785499caa619ee73939267035f690bdae971636c3e5cd4de0dc4cd2f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 0.86], [4, 0.86, 1.24], [5, 1.24, 1.46], [6, 1.46, 1.76], [7, 1.76, 2.1], [8, 2.1, 2.28], [9, 2.28, 2.52], [10, 2.52, 2.88], [11, 3.4, 3.52], [12, 3.52, 3.82], [13, 3.82, 4.0], [14, 4.0, 4.28], [15, 4.28, 4.56], [16, 4.56, 4.7], [17, 4.7, 4.88], [18, 4.88, 5.04], [19, 5.04, 5.34]]}, {"text": "Conclusion", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4888e403da94f4096ce831f4178717ca07d3749347a8d426ba8b09313a16232c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.64]]}, {"text": "Like always, feel free to hit me up in the chat.", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a13b5a4880be5a860d09b0379c65f12cd161b7e9c37719e8513d42464535f8ae.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.7], [2, 1.04, 1.14], [3, 1.14, 1.36], [4, 1.36, 1.46], [5, 1.46, 1.6], [6, 1.6, 1.74], [7, 1.74, 1.92], [8, 1.92, 2.04], [9, 2.04, 2.14], [10, 2.14, 2.4]]}, {"text": "My chat tool is hooked into Google Talk, free too drop me a message if you have any questions.", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ddefd002c6bb373133afbeb83bdb1dca114f9b9bd9215b13bfed3fe4aadbd867.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.38], [6, 1.38, 1.7], [7, 1.7, 2.0], [8, 2.48, 2.6], [10, 2.82, 3.1], [11, 3.1, 3.26], [12, 3.26, 3.32], [13, 3.32, 3.66], [14, 3.66, 3.98], [15, 3.98, 4.08], [16, 4.08, 4.24], [17, 4.24, 4.38], [18, 4.38, 4.8]]}, {"text": "Cheers.", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3c356ca8be70b6ecabb54a5e0bad26f62259567f53617569cc8ea6a931b70b12.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3]]}]}